{
  "name": "Weathered Timber and Curved Iron Park Bench",
  "rationale": "A full-scale, stationary park bench with five separate seat slats, three inclined backrest slats, timber arm caps, and paired iron frames. Segmented round iron beams form curved legs and reclining back supports. Four ground-contact shoes and a transverse stretcher stabilize the frame. Exposed bolt heads identify timber-to-frame connections. Muted, individually varied timber colors suggest sun bleaching and worn finish; dark iron and dull hardware remain readable without excessive contrast. Openings between slats, beneath the arms, and between the legs are preserved. Seat timber tops are at 0.44 m. Beam start and end coordinates are absolute; beam locations mark their midpoints.",
